{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1777590915,"nonce":"GaRJAKg+bPneeF6Ga2DIn2mvMX4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABA_xx-A","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/117","origin":"github"},"title":"sbg driver: `ros_standard: true` not producing standard ROS topics on BizzyBoat","message":"## Summary\n\nThe boat-side SBG Ellipse-D driver YAML\n([`bizzyboat_project11/config/sbg_ellipse_d.yaml`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/blob/jazzy/bizzyboat_project11/config/sbg_ellipse_d.yaml))\nsets `output.ros_standard: true` (line 55), which per the\n`sbg_ros2_driver` documentation should cause the driver to publish a\nparallel set of **standard-typed** ROS messages alongside the\nSBG-specific `sbg_driver/Sbg*` ones. **The standard topics are not on\nthe wire** — confirmed via the cod rock bag analysis (#104).\n\n## Evidence\n\nThe `udp_bridge` on gabby tracked **289 known topics** during the\n2026-04-29 cod rock survey (`/bizzy/udp_bridge/bridge_info.topics`).\nFiltering for SBG-related and `/imu/`-pattern entries:\n\n**SBG-specific (present, all 9):**\n\n```\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/ekf_nav      (sbg_driver/SbgEkfNav)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/ekf_quat     (sbg_driver/SbgEkfQuat)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_hdt      (sbg_driver/SbgGpsHdt)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_pos      (sbg_driver/SbgGpsPos)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/gps_vel      (sbg_driver/SbgGpsVel)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu_data     (sbg_driver/SbgImuData)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/mag          (sbg_driver/SbgMag)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/status       (sbg_driver/SbgStatus)\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/utc_time     (sbg_driver/SbgUtcTime)\n```\n\n**Standard-typed (expected if `ros_standard: true` were applied,\nabsent):**\n\n```\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/data        (sensor_msgs/Imu)         ✗\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/nav_sat_fix (sensor_msgs/NavSatFix)   ✗\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/odometry    (nav_msgs/Odometry)       ✗\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/velocity    (geometry_msgs/TwistStamped) ✗\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/mag         (sensor_msgs/MagneticField) ✗\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/temp        (sensor_msgs/Temperature) ✗\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/utc_ref     (sensor_msgs/TimeReference) ✗\n/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/pos_ecef    (geometry_msgs/PointStamped) ✗\n```\n\nThe only `/imu/...` topics in the bridge's known list are mavros'\nown (`/bizzy/mavros/imu/data`, `/bizzy/mavros/imu/data_raw`, etc.) —\nnot SBG.\n\nSo the YAML says `ros_standard: true`, but at runtime the driver\nbehaves as if `ros_standard: false`.\n\n## Likely cause\n\nThe `sbg_ellipse_d.yaml` uses the global wildcard pattern:\n\n```yaml\n/**:\n  ros__parameters:\n    driver:\n      frequency: 400\n    ...\n    output:\n      time_reference: \"ros\"\n      ros_standard: true\n```\n\nThe `sbg_ros2_driver`'s `sbg_device` node may not be honouring\nparameters loaded under `/**:` for this specific knob, OR the\nlaunch file's namespace-push (`PushRosNamespace('sensors/sbg')` in\n`sbg_launch.py`) is interacting with how the driver looks up the\n`output.ros_standard` key. This is similar in shape to the\n`mavros local_position` `child_frame_id` issue in #104's wrap-up\n(commit `d40845e`) where a YAML namespace pattern didn't reach the\nplugin's actual node namespace and the fix was a no-op until a\nTF-bridge workaround landed.\n\nQuick check next time the SBG driver is up:\n\n```bash\nros2 topic list | grep '/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/'\nros2 param get /bizzy/sensors/sbg/sbg_device output.ros_standard\nros2 param dump /bizzy/sensors/sbg/sbg_device\n```\n\nIf the param is `False` despite the YAML saying `true`, the YAML\nisn't reaching the node. If the param is `True` but the topics\naren't on the wire, that's a different bug (driver not honouring\nthe param after loading it).\n\n## Why it matters\n\nBag analysis tooling in `marine_tools` (see\n[`marine_tools#6`](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/6))\nbenefits from being able to consume **standard** ROS message types\nrather than custom `sbg_driver/Sbg*` types — the package can then\nwork without an `sbg_driver` runtime dependency, and the same plot\ngenerators keep working when the SBG comes off the boat at the end\nof the class loan (mavros publishes the same standard types on its\nown topics).\n\nmavros already provides everything the boat needs today\n(`/bizzy/mavros/imu/data`, `/bizzy/mavros/global_position/raw/fix`,\n`/bizzy/mavros/local_position/odom`, etc., all confirmed on the\nwire), so this is **not** blocking. But fixing it would give a\nclean cross-check between the two nav stacks for as long as SBG is\non the boat.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `ros2 topic list | grep '/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu/'` shows the\n  expected standard-typed topics with the SBG driver running.\n- The standard topics carry the same data the SBG-specific topics do\n  (cross-check against `/bizzy/sensors/sbg/imu_data` for orientation,\n  `gps_pos` for lat/lon, etc.).\n- Boat-side `bizzyboat.yaml` logger is updated to record the standard\n  topics (separate follow-up — pointless until the topics exist on\n  the wire).\n\n## References\n\n- [`#104`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/104)\n  — 2026-04-29 deployment whose bag confirmed the absence\n- Cod rock bag bridge_info evidence: dev log\n  `docs/logs/2026/2026-04-29_dev_logs.md` (Issues encountered + the\n  bag inspection summarised in the `marine_tools#6` review thread)\n- [`marine_tools#6`](https://github.com/rolker/marine_tools/pull/6)\n  — bag_analysis PR; this is what surfaced the question of which\n  message types are durable vs. SBG-specific\n- [`#110`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/110),\n  [`#111`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/111),\n  [`#112`](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/112)\n  — the existing SBG / nav follow-up trio\n- Similar precedent: PR #98 commit `d40845e` (mavros `local_position`\n  `child_frame_id` no-op due to YAML-namespace mismatch) — same\n  failure mode shape\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}